Stage 3 deliberately has **no** `synthdefs/ji_freqset_receiver.scd`; the OSC
receiver in `test_bridge.scd` supersedes the old server-buffer lookup. The
12-slot Hz Buffer mirror is written for future stages but is not read by any
SynthDef yet.

Stage 4 likewise has **no** `synthdefs/ji_autotune_dual.scd`: it starts two
instances of the verified `\ji_autotune_ch` graph, one per input channel, so
there is no second autotune DSP definition to maintain.

### 4.4 Startup order (Stage 5 onward)

1. Human verifies Aggregate Device and BlackHole exist (Audio MIDI Setup).
2. Human opens Ableton, configures input as BlackHole 64ch, enables 16 input channels, arms MPE track(s).
3. Human launches SC IDE, evaluates `startup.scd` (server boots, buses allocated, SynthDefs loaded).
4. Human evaluates `test_autotune.scd` (Stage 1), `test_bridge.scd` (Stage 3), or `test_dual_loop.scd` (Stage 4).
5. Human launches Python bridge (`python control/ji_bridge.py`).
6. Human launches UI (`python ui/ji_ui.py`, Stage 9).

