## 5. Global Contract

This contract applies to **all stages**. Included verbatim in every agent prompt.

### 5.1 Naming conventions

| Entity | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| SynthDef name | `\ji_` prefix, camelCase | `\ji_autotune_ch` |
| Global variable | `~ji_*` | `~ji_autotune_freq1` |
| Control bus | `~ji_<subsystem>_<param>` | `~ji_tartini_freq1` |
| Audio bus | `~ji_audio_*` | `~ji_audio_loop1` |
| Buffer | `~ji_buf_*` | `~ji_buf_loop1` |
| SynthDef argument | camelCase | `retuneTime`, `inBus` |
| OSC address | `/ji/<subsystem>/<action>` | `/ji/mutation/trigger` |
| Python module | `snake_case.py` | `mutation.py` |
| Python class | `PascalCase` | `MutationEngine` |
| MIDI map file | `config/*.json` | `config/midi_map.json` |

### 5.2 Bus allocation (cumulative, never reassign)

| Bus | Name | Stage | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | `~ji_tartini_freq1` | 0 | Debug tracker freq, ch 0 |
| 1 | `~ji_tartini_freq2` | 0 | Debug tracker freq, ch 1 |
| 2 | `~ji_tartini_hasfreq1` | 0 | Debug confidence, ch 0 |
| 3 | `~ji_tartini_hasfreq2` | 0 | Debug confidence, ch 1 |
| 4 | `~ji_cpu` | 0 | System CPU |
| 5 | `~ji_autotune_freq1` | 1 | Autotune tracker freq, ch 0 |
| 6 | `~ji_autotune_hasfreq1` | 1 | Autotune confidence, ch 0 |
| 7 | `~ji_autotune_target1` | 1 | Target freq, ch 0 |
| 8 | `~ji_autotune_freq2` | 4 | Autotune tracker freq, ch 1 |
| 9 | `~ji_autotune_hasfreq2` | 4 | Autotune confidence, ch 1 |
| 10 | `~ji_autotune_target2` | 4 | Target freq, ch 1 |
| 11–14 | `~ji_loop_freq1..4` | 4 | Loop tracker freqs |
| 15–18 | `~ji_loop_hasfreq1..4` | 4 | Loop confidences |

**Audio bus allocation:** Stage 4 keeps 0–1 input and 0–1 output (SC reuses indices); mono loops sum to output 0 or 1, so no internal loop audio buses are allocated. The Stage 5 plan reserves loop audio buses 10–17 (4 stereo pairs) for separate Ableton streams. VST/MPE do not consume global audio bus indices.

### 5.3 Audio-thread rule (inviolable)

**Never modify a running Synth's internal structure at runtime.** Structural changes only via SynthDef recompilation + node replacement with crossfade, or allocating a new node and freeing the old one. Parameter changes via `Synth.set` and buffer content via `Buffer.setn` are safe.

### 5.4 MIDI-thread rule

MPE MIDI output must not block the audio thread or the main control thread. Use a dedicated MIDI-sending thread or `mido`'s non-blocking mode. Voice allocation and pitch-bend calculation happen in the control layer, never in a SynthDef.

### 5.5 Output format (for agent-generated code)

1. Fenced code blocks per file, each preceded by `### FILE: <path>`.
2. `### SELF-REVIEW` section (mandatory — see §10.4).
3. `### ASSUMPTIONS` section (≤5 bullets).

