## 7. Data Formats & Interfaces

### 7.1 OSC address map (cumulative)

| Address | Args | Direction | Stage |
|---|---|---|---|
| `/ji/mutation/trigger` | none | Control → Bridge | 2 ✅ |
| `/ji/mutation/octave` | none | Control → Bridge | 2 ✅ |
| `/ji/mutation/set_randomness` | float [0,1] | Control → Bridge | 2 ✅ |
| `/ji/mutation/set_dissonance_bias` | float [-1,1] | Control → Bridge | 2 ✅ |
| `/ji/mutation/set_stepwise_bias` | float [0,1] | Control → Bridge | 2 ✅ |
| `/ji/mutation/set_glide_time` | float ≥0 | Control → Bridge | 2 ✅ |
| `/ji/mutation/set_change_count` | number (clamped 1..max_changes) | Control → Bridge | 3.5 🟡 |
| `/ji/mutation/set_temperature` | float [0,1] | Control → Bridge | 3.5 🟡 |
| `/ji/mutation/set_anchor_mobility` | float [0,1] | Control → Bridge | 3.5 🟡 |
| `/ji/freqset/update` | [float fundamental, float glide_time, float ratio_1 … ratio_N] | Bridge → sclang | 3 ✅ |
| `/ji/freqset/changed` | float[] | Bridge → UI | 9 |
| `/ji/autotune/set` | [string, float] | Control → Server | 7 |
| `/ji/loop/record` | int (index) | Control → Server | 8 (not in Stage 4) |
| `/ji/loop/stop` | int | Control → Server | 8 (not in Stage 4) |
| `/ji/loop/play` | int | Control → Server | 8 (not in Stage 4) |
| `/ji/loop/clear` | int | Control → Server | 8 (not in Stage 4) |
| `/ji/granular/trigger` | [float, float] | Control → Server | 8 |
| `/ji/midi/map` | [int, string] | Control → Bridge | 8 |
| `/ji/bass/trigger` | none | Control → Bridge | 6 |
| `/ji/bass/set_note` | int (MIDI note) | Control → Bridge | 6 |
| `/ji/bass/set_glide` | float (sec) | Control → Bridge | 6 |
| `/ji/bass/set_interval` | int | Control → Bridge | 6 |
| `/ji/bass/current` | float (Hz) | Bridge → UI | 6 |
| `/ji/mpe/set_bend_range` | float (semitones) | Control → Bridge | 6 |
| `/ji/cpu` | float | Server → UI | 9 |
| `/ji/event/mutation` | [float, float, float[]] | Bridge → Visual | 10 |
| `/ji/event/pitchclass` | [int, int, float] | Bridge → Visual | 10 |
| `/ji/event/grain` | [float, float] | Bridge → Visual | 10 |
| `/ji/event/loop` | [int, string] | Bridge → Visual | 10 |
| `/ji/event/bass` | float (Hz) | Bridge → Visual | 10 |

Stage 3 does **not** send `/ji/mutation/apply` or any message directly to scsynth. The complete set is sent on `/ji/freqset/update`; sclang applies it to the verified nearest-class lookup. A multi-edit batch sends one `/ji/freqset/update` with the final set and one glide time, not intermediate sets. Rows for later stages remain future work.

### 7.2 FrequencySet (control-layer object)

```python
{
    "ratios": [1.0, 1.125, 1.25, 1.333, 1.5, 1.666, 1.875],  # octave-reduced
    "fundamental": 220.0,
    "targetSize": 7,
    "minSize": 3,
    "maxSize": 12,
    "anchorRatio": 1.0,
    "analysisVoicing": {1.0: 0, 1.125: 0, 1.25: 0, ...}
}
```

`analysisVoicing` is a representative class → octave map for scoring, not a global register constraint. Live input uses its own octave. The bridge sends octave-reduced ratios plus fundamental and glide to sclang; sclang writes the Hz mirror via `Buffer.setn`. That mirror is not read by any SynthDef in Stage 3.

The runtime event shapes are:

```python
MutationEvent(
    removed_ratio=None | float,
    new_ratio=None | float,
    glide_time=float,
    reason="added" | "removed" | "replaced" | "stepwise",
    new_octave=None | int,
    removed_octave=None | int,
)

MutationBatch(
    events=tuple[MutationEvent, ...],  # already applied
    glide_time=float,
)

OctaveEvent(
    ratio=float,
    old_octave=int,
    new_octave=int,
    glide_time=float,
    reason="octave_up" | "octave_down",
)
```

### 7.3 Loop buffer file format

48 kHz, stereo, 32-bit float, `.aiff`. Naming: `loops/loop_<index>_<timestamp>.aiff`.

### 7.4 MIDI mapping file

`config/midi_map.json`:
```json
{
    "note_60": "mutate",
    "note_62": "mutate_stepwise",
    "note_64": "mutate_random",
    "note_65": "bass_trigger",
    "cc_1": "randomness",
    "cc_2": "dissonance_bias"
}
```

### 7.5 MPE configuration file (Stage 6)

`config/mpe_config.json`:
```json
{
    "port_name": "IAC Driver Bus 1",
    "master_channel": 1,
    "bass_channel": 2,
    "bend_range_semitones": 48,
    "bass_base_note": 36,
    "bass_glide_time": 0.5,
    "bass_mutation_interval": 8,
    "bass_must_be_set_member": true
}
```

