## 9. Current Implementation Status

| Stage | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | ✅ Complete | Environment verified. Tartini works. 2ch I/O passes. |
| 1 | ✅ Complete | Autotune sounds great. retuneTime works. CPU < 20%. |
| 2 | ✅ Complete | Decentralised mutation engine + OSC listener. Harness passes. |
| 3 | ✅ Complete | Bridge accepted by owner: audio and Python↔sclang working. |
| 3.5 | 🟡 Implemented — awaiting audio acceptance | Mutation batch width, temperature, anchor mobility. Python harness passes. |
| 4 | 🟡 Implemented — awaiting audio acceptance | Dual live autotune, dry mono loop recorder, four loop voices with independent Tartini/PitchShift chains, broadcast glide. |
| 5 | ⬜ Pending | Ableton routing. Requires BlackHole install. |
| 6 | ⬜ Pending | MPE + bass/drone. Requires IAC Driver enabled, calibration. |
| 7 | ⬜ Optional | SC-side VST hosting. May be skipped if Ableton handles VSTs. |
| 8 | ⬜ Pending | MIDI mutation + granular FX. |
| 9 | ⬜ Pending | PyQt6 UI. |
| 10 | ⬜ Deferred | Visual event broadcast. |

**What Stage 0 verified:**
- SC 3.15 dev from source runs on Apple Silicon.
- sc3-plugins + Tartini load correctly (ABI compatible).
- 2-channel audio interface connected and functional.
- Buses 0–4 allocated and readable.
- Tartini tracks guitar and voice accurately.
- Passthrough audio clean.

**What Stage 1 verified:**
- `\ji_autotune_ch` SynthDef compiles and runs.
- Chromatic input snaps to 7-note JI set (verified by ear and post-window log).
- `retuneTime` audibly changes glide (0.005 = snap, 0.5 = portamento).
- No clicks at note boundaries.
- CPU < 20% with one channel active.
- **Overall: "sounds great" per project owner.**

**What Stage 2 verified:**
- Octave-equivalent ratios fold and deduplicate correctly.
- Set size breathes around 7 (observed 6–8) and never exceeds 12.
- A full 12-class set never dead-ends; removals and replacements occur.
- The class field keeps drifting instead of converging to a fixed chord.
- Stepwise replacements stay within ±1.5 semitones.
- Octave moves do not alter class membership or set size.
- The anchor is retained far more often than ordinary classes (observed ~4.5% removal rate versus uniform), and re-anchors when removed.
- `ALL TESTS PASSED` under CPython 3.12 WASM; native `uv` command provided.

**What Stage 3 verified (owner accepted):**
- Python bridge sends the full set plus glide at startup and after every mutation.
- sclang validates the update, applies the set, writes the 12-slot Hz mirror, and reuses the Stage 1 lookup.
- A removed/replaced held class retunes on the next 20 Hz lookup tick, with `retuneTime = max(glide, 0.005)` set before `targetFreq`.
- Octave events and `new_octave` remain analysis-only; live input uses its own octave.
- Owner reports audio and Python↔sclang communication working.

**What Stage 3.5 implements (awaiting audio acceptance):**
- `change_count`/`max_changes` batches (default max 3), applied atomically, one final set update.
- `temperature` broadening the palette/relaxing scoring and flattening rank selection.
- `anchor_mobility` 0..1: anchor fixed, old 1/4 default, or no precedence with random re-anchoring.
- `test_mutation_controls.py` passes under CPython 3.12/Pyodide.

**What Stage 4 implements (awaiting audio acceptance):**
- `startup.scd` allocates the cumulative buses 0–18 and reports the full map.
- Two independent live autotune voices on input 0/out 0 and input 1/out 1, each with its own tracker buses and target.
- `\ji_looper_recorder` captures the dry, pre-autotune input into a mono buffer (overwrite, no overdub) with a `run` gate and an explicit stop path.
- `\ji_looper_player` runs `PlayBuf → Tartini → PitchShift` per loop, writes loop tracker buses 11–18, and takes `targetFreq`/`retuneTime` from sclang only.
- One 20 Hz lookup services every active live/loop voice with the verified nearest-class arithmetic and a per-voice `lastTarget`.
- Set updates broadcast the event glide to all active voices; a mutation can retune both live channels and all playing loops without replay.
- Loop transport is sclang-only; no Python loop OSC control and no new Python protocol.

**What is still unverified:**
- **Stage 4 audible acceptance** (dual independent autotune, raw loop recording, per-loop retune without restart, loop start/stop clicks, measured CPU with 2 live + 2 loops).
- **Stage 3.5 audible acceptance** (batch width, temperature, anchor mobility).
- Actual per-voice octave allocation and audio retuning (Stage 3/4).
- Ableton audio routing (Stage 5).
- IAC Driver MIDI output (Stage 6).
- MPE pitch bend calibration (Stage 6).
- Multi-channel audio stability over long sessions (Stage 5).
- VSTPlugin SC-side loading (Stage 7, likely moot if Ableton hosts VSTs).
- Real-time performance latency under full load (Stage 9).

